t Myers, FL\", fontsize = \"14\")\n","plt.legend()\n","\n","# Get the change in temperature over the next 25 years\n","change = yvals[163] - yvals[133]\n","change2 = yvals2[80] - yvals2[50]\n","\n","# Slope is negative so get absolute value to print\n","change = abs(change)\n","change2 = abs(change2)\n","\n","# Print the change\n","print(f\"Using data since 1892, the number of heating degree days is expected to decrease by {change:.3f} days over the next 30 years\")\n","print(f\"Using data from the last 50 years, the number of heating degree days is expected to decrease by {change2:.3f} days over the next 30 years\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"SK24_OShKM74"},"source":["The projection above for the heating degree days in Fort Myers over the next 30 years shows that heating degree days are decreasing very quickly; they are expected to become near zero by the year 2055. Using the trendline over the last 50 years, there is a projected decrease of 136 heating degree days for the next 30 years. This means that energy required for heating buildings in Fort Myers, FL will become almost zero in the coming decades, leading to decreased energy consumption, and decreased energy pollution, which in turn will help reduce the rate of global warming."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"PimpCh-e05iD"},"source":["##CDD - Cooling Degree Days"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"FeiJvJj3snnR"},"source":["The CDD dataset measures how many degrees the average daily temperature rises above a base comfort level, which indicates how much energy might be needed for cooling. Trends in CDD over time show whether a region is experiencing hotter conditions and longer warm seasons. This information is important because rising CDD values signal increasing heat intensity due to climate change, impacting energy demand and ecosystems. Projecting future CDD levels helps cities and planners prepare for risks that might ensue from future CDD levels. Studying past and future trends, we can better understand and plan for the effects caused by global warming."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":635},"id":"Q2bU8FYDn8lk","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1765349557550,"user_tz":360,"elapsed":353,"user":{"displayName":"David Gray","userId":"09426756811334309153"}},"outputId":"ac11f5ba-3ed6-4aa8-8861-3816a2d721f2"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stderr","text":["/tmp/ipython-input-1747584336.py:7: FutureWarning: The 'delim_whitespace' keyword in pd.read_csv is deprecated and will be removed in a future version. Use ``sep='\\s+'`` instead\n","  return pd.read_csv(filename, delim_whitespace=True)\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Slope of the entire dataset: 0.020 CDD/year\n","Slope over the past 50 years: 0.021 CDD/year\n"]}],"source":["# Will Shoaf\n","import pandas as pd\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import numpy as np\n","\n","def load_data(filename):\n","    return pd.read_csv(filename, delim_whitespace=True)\n","\n","def split_data(df, cutoff_year=2020):\n","    present_data = df[df['Year'] <= cutoff_year]\n","    future_data = df[df['Year'] > cutoff_year]\n","    return present_data, future_data\n","\n","def calculate_trendline(x, y):\n","    slope, intercept = np.polyfit(x, y, 1)\n","    trend = slope * x + intercept\n","    return slope, intercept, trend\n","\n","def plot_cdd(present_df):\n","    plt.figure(figsize=(10,6))\n","\n","    plt.plot(present_df['Year'], present_df['Annual'], 'k-', label=\"Data\")\n","\n","    slope_all, _, trend_all = calculate_trendline(present_df['Year'], present_df['Annual'])\n","    plt.plot(present_df['Year'], trend_all, 'r-', label=\"Trendline over entire data\")\n","\n","    last_50_years = present_df[present_df['Year'] > (present_df['Year'].max() - 50)]\n","    slope_50, _, trend_50 = calculate_trendline(last_50_years['Year'], last_50_years['Annual'])\n","    plt.plot(last_50_years['Year'], trend_50, 'b-', label=\"Trendline over past 50 Years\")\n","\n","    plt.xlabel(\"Year\", fontsize=11)\n","    plt.ylabel(\"Cooling Degree Days\", fontsize=11)\n","    plt.title(\"Average Cooling Degree Days per Year in Fort Myers, FL\", fontsize=14)\n","    plt.legend()\n","    plt.show()\n","\n","    print(f\"Slope of the entire dataset: {slope_all:.3f} CDD/year\")\n","    print(f\"Slope over the past 50 years: {slope_50:.3f} CDD/year\")\n","\n","if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n","    data_file = \"fortMyersCDD.txt\"\n","    df = load_data(data_file)\n","    present, future = split_data(df)\n","    plot_cdd(present)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":635},"id":"93VPCYTtrUQC","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1765349560215,"user_tz":360,"elapsed":237,"user":{"displayName":"David Gray","userId":"09426756811334309153"}},"outputId":"545bf74b-ef96-4734-b166-3df96efdeedc"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stderr","text":["/tmp/ipython-input-577236479.py:7: FutureWarning: The 'delim_whitespace' keyword in pd.read_csv is deprecated and will be removed in a future version. Use ``sep='\\s+'`` instead\n","  return pd.read_csv(filename, delim_whitespace=True)\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Slope since 2000: 0.107 CDD/year\n","Slope over last 20 years: 0.116 CDD/year\n"]}],"source":["#Will Shoad\n","import pandas as pd\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import numpy as np\n","\n","def load_data(filename):\n","    return pd.read_csv(filename, delim_whitespace=True)\n","\n","def calculate_trendline(x, y, future_years=50):\n","    slope, intercept = np.polyfit(x, y, 1)\n","    x_extended = np.arange(x.min(), x.max() + future_years + 1)\n","    trend_extended = slope * x_extended + intercept\n","    return slope, intercept, x_extended, trend_extended\n","\n","def plot_cdd_projection(df, start_year=2000, future_years=50):\n","    df_recent = df[df['Year'] >= start_year]\n","\n","    plt.figure(figsize=(10,6))\n","    plt.plot(df_recent['Year'], df_recent['Annual'], 'k-', label=\"Data (2000+)\")\n","\n","    slope_all, _, x_ext_all, trend_all = calculate_trendline(df_recent['Year'], df_recent['Annual'], future_years)\n","    plt.plot(x_ext_all, trend_all, 'r', label=f\"Trendline since 2000 (projected 50 yrs into future)\")\n","\n","    last_20 = df_recent[df_recent['Year'] > (df_recent['Year'].max() - 20)]\n","    slope_20, _, x_ext_20, trend_20 = calculate_trendline(last_20['Year'], last_20['Annual'], future_years)\n","    plt.plot(x_ext_20, trend_20, 'b', label=f\"Trendline over last 20 yrs (projected 50 yrs into future)\")\n","\n","    plt.xlabel(\"Year\", fontsize=11)\n","    plt.ylabel(\"Cooling Degree Days\", fontsize=11)\n","    plt.title(f\"Cooling Degree Days in Fort Myers, FL Since 2000 + Future Predicitions\", fontsize=14)\n","    plt.legend()\n","    plt.show()\n","\n","    print(f\"Slope since {start_year}: {slope_all:.3f} CDD/year\")\n","    print(f\"Slope over last 20 years: {slope_20:.3f} CDD/year\")\n","\n","if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n","    data_file = \"fortMyersCDD.txt\"\n","    df = load_data(data_file)\n","    plot_cdd_projection(df, start_year=2000, future_years=50)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"ttcUeDE5nC5S"},"source":["## GDD - Growing Degree Days"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"5Rf3-Ra4GN88"},"source":["A Growing Degree Day measures how much warmth accumulates over time, based on daily temperatures. It’s used to track how quickly plants and insects grow.\n","\n","**Why This Matters**\n","\n","Rising GDDs mean an area is getting warmer. This affects:\n","\n","**Crops:** Longer growing seasons and shifting crop zones\n","\n","**Ecosystems:** Changes in plant and animal life cycles\n","\n","**Pests:** More rapid growth and wider spread of insects\n","\n","Increasing GDDs are a clear sign of a warming climate and its impact on natural systems."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"fKNK-LgXlGCq"},"source":["### **Trends Over Time**\n","---"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":642},"id":"MtR7gM3IlLcy","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1765349563771,"user_tz":360,"elapsed":268,"user":{"displayName":"David Gray","userId":"09426756811334309153"}},"outputId":"caebf490-d695-4918-f344-a345c0685fda"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Slope of all years: 0.023 GDD/year\n","Slope of last 50 years: 0.044 GDD/year\n"]}],"source":["# WILL MORGAN\n","# import libraries\n","import pandas as pd\n","import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","# read data\n","df = pd.read_csv(\"fortMyersGDD.txt\", sep=r\"\\s+\")\n","df = df.sort_values(\"Year\")\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10,6))\n","\n","# annual values\n","plt.plot(df[\"Year\"], df[\"Annual\"], \"k-\", label=\"Data\")\n","\n","# all years slope\n","slope_all, intercept_all = np.polyfit(df[\"Year\"], df[\"Annual\"], 1)\n","fit_all = slope_all * df[\"Year\"] + intercept_all\n","plt.plot(df[\"Year\"], fit_all, \"r-\", label=\"Trendline all years\")\n","\n","# last 50 years slope\n","cutoff = df[\"Year\"].max() - 50\n","recent = df[df[\"Year\"] > cutoff]\n","slope_50, intercept_50 = np.polyfit(recent[\"Year\"], recent[\"Annual\"], 1)\n","fit_50 = slope_50 * recent[\"Year\"] + intercept_50\n","plt.plot(recent[\"Year\"], fit_50, \"b-\", label=\"Trendline last 50 years\")\n","\n","# labels\n","plt.xlabel(\"Year\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"Growing Degree Days\")\n","plt.title(\"Total Growing Degree Days per Year in Fort Myers, FL\")\n","plt.legend()\n","plt.grid(True)\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n","\n","# print slopes\n","print(f\"Slope of all years: {slope_all:.3f} GDD/year\")\n","print(f\"Slope of last 50 years: {slope_50:.3f} GDD/year\")\n","\n","\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"roZvRH0NKSWx"},"source":["The graph shows that the average number of GDDs per month has steadily increased over the past 50 years, meaning the region has been consistently warming.\n","\n","**Why this matters:**\n","\n","This steady rise is clear evidence of long-term climate change in the area.\n","\n","Warmer conditions make crops develop faster but can also lead to more heat stress and reduced yields.\n","\n","Ecosystems are shifting as plants, animals, and pests adjust to longer, warmer growing seasons."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"8Iivgwj6lnhy"},"source":["# Future Projections\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":642},"id":"LDf_01uveLFv","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1765349566519,"user_tz":360,"elapsed":260,"user":{"displayName":"David Gray","userId":"09426756811334309153"}},"outputId":"c4ffec79-da1a-482a-d2b2-a7111af42fba"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Using all years, GDD is expected to increase by 0.691 over the next 30 years.\n","Using last 50 years, GDD is expected to increase by 1.310 over the next 30 years.\n"]}],"source":["# WILL MORGAN\n","# Import libraries\n","import pandas as pd\n","import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","# read data\n","df = pd.read_csv(\"fortMyersGDD.txt\", sep=r\"\\s+\")\n","df = df.sort_values(\"Year\")\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10,6))\n","\n","# data line\n","plt.plot(df[\"Year\"], df[\"Annual\"], \"k-\", label=\"Data\")\n","\n","# trend from all years\n","slope_all, intercept_all = np.polyfit(df[\"Year\"], df[\"Annual\"], 1)\n","x_all = np.arange(df[\"Year\"].min(), 2056)\n","y_all = slope_all * x_all + intercept_all\n","plt.plot(x_all, y_all, \"r-\", label=\"Trendline all years\")\n","\n","# trend from last 50 years\n","cutoff = df[\"Year\"].max() - 50\n","recent = df[df[\"Year\"] > cutoff]\n","slope_50, intercept_50 = np.polyfit(recent[\"Year\"], recent[\"Annual\"], 1)\n","x_50 = np.arange(recent[\"Year\"].min(), 2056)\n","y_50 = slope_50 * x_50 + intercept_50\n","plt.plot(x_50, y_50, \"b-\", label=\"Trendline last 50 years\")\n","\n","# labels\n","plt.xlabel(\"Year\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"Growing Degree Days\")\n","plt.title(\"Projection of Future Growing Degree Days in Fort Myers, FL\")\n","plt.legend()\n","plt.grid(True)\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n","\n","# change over next 30 years using slopes\n","start_year = 2025\n","end_year = 2055\n","\n","proj_start_all = slope_all * start_year + intercept_all\n","proj_end_all = slope_all * end_year + intercept_all\n","delta_all = proj_end_all - proj_start_all\n","\n","proj_start_50 = slope_50 * start_year + intercept_50\n","proj_end_50 = slope_50 * end_year + intercept_50\n","delta_50 = proj_end_50 - proj_start_50\n","\n","direction_all = \"increase\" if delta_all > 0 else \"decrease\"\n","direction_50 = \"increase\" if delta_50 > 0 else \"decrease\"\n","\n","print(f\"Using all years, GDD is expected to {direction_all} by {abs(delta_all):.3f} over the next 30 years.\")\n","print(f\"Using last 50 years, GDD is expected to {direction_50} by {abs(delta_50):.3f} over the next 30 years.\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"tp9LnHs5GFje"},"source":["\n","\n","**Future projections:**\n","The data indicates that GDDs are expected to keep increasing. This suggests continued regional warming, longer growing seasons, and ongoing changes in both agriculture and natural ecosystems."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"NZ